.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH FATHOM_NOTE_ANSWER 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-note\-answer \- Answer a question or close a follow\-up by appending the note that closes it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom note answer\fR [\fB\-\-author\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\fR] [\fB\-\-kind\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR> <\fITEXT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Answer a question or close a follow\-up by appending the note that closes it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-author\fR \fI<AUTHOR>\fR
Who is answering
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\fR \fI<AGENT>\fR
Record the answer as an agent\*(Aqs act on someone\*(Aqs behalf
.TP
\fB\-\-kind\fR \fI<KIND>\fR [default: decision]
The kind of the answering note: a `decision` is an answer that settles it, an `annotation` is an answer that informs it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
The question or follow\-up being answered (`nt\-…`)
.TP
<\fITEXT\fR>
The answer
